    "knowledge_point": "Perpendicular Vectors",
    "problem": "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$",
    "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+0\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{4}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}}d \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
